vatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13615376?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk","html_url":"https://github.com/kmuthukk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-09-28T06:18:46Z","updated_at":"2018-09-28T06:18:46Z","body":"@robertpang \r\n\r\nWhen the system is doing writes after the restart, the aforementioned yb-tserver logs continue to spew the following:\r\n\r\n```\r\nWhen I run the CUSI (unique sec idx) workload after restart... it is still spewing these errors like crazy:\r\n\r\nE0928 06:11:35.523056 23094 process_context.cc:180] SQL Error: Tablet Not Found. Not found: Failed Write(tablet: 1cb7e3157d184fd4b3ca2249888534b0, num_ops: 1, num_attempts: 1) to tablet 1cb7e3157d184fd4b3ca2249888534b0 on tablet server { uuid: 2929187a2a994a6194f0b8484f24dc5d private: [host: \"172.151.44.11\" port: 9100] cloud_info: placement_cloud: \"aws\" placement_region: \"us-west\" placement_zone: \"us-west-2b\" after 1 attempt(s): Index id 495d9aee5ad94c93aeeb7800093c83f5 not found\r\nINSERT INTO CassandraUniqueSecondaryIndex (k, v) VALUES (?, ?);\r\n      ^^^^\r\nE0928 06:11:35.523073 23116 process_context.cc:180] SQL Error: Tablet Not Found. Not found: Failed Write(tablet: 37b0c2ab95474c9586cf16b2425c781b, num_ops: 1, num_attempts: 1) to tablet 37b0c2ab95474c9586cf16b2425c781b on tablet server { uuid: 2929187a2a994a6194f0b8484f24dc5d private: [host: \"172.151.44.11\" port: 9100] cloud_info: placement_cloud: \"aws\" placement_region: \"us-west\" placement_zone: \"us-west-2b\" after 1 attempt(s): Index id 495d9aee5ad94c93aeeb7800093c83f5 not found\r\nINSERT INTO CassandraUniqueSecondaryIndex (k, v) VALUES (?, ?);\r\n      ^^^^\r\nE0928 06:11:35.523399 23013 process_context.cc:180] SQL Error: Tablet Not Found. Not found: Failed Write(tablet: 6bf7d37414e1473f845032da864ec4b3, num_ops: 1, num_attempts: 1) to tablet 6bf7d37414e1473f845032da864ec4b3 on tablet server { uuid: 2929187a2a994a6194f0b8484f24dc5d private: [host: \"172.151.44.11\" port: 9100] cloud_info: placement_cloud: \"aws\" placement_region: \"us-west\" placement_zone: \"us-west-2b\" after 1 attempt(s): Index id 495d9aee5ad94c93aeeb7800093c83f5 not found\r\n```\r\n\r\nThey are all complaining about the same \"Index id 495d9aee5ad94c93aeeb7800093c83f5\" which is the \"table\" id of the index. Is it possible that the logic similar to ybclient that you have for TServer to do index update RPC calls is not able to refresh its cache?\r\n\r\nWe should do the classic 1-time refresh of the meta-data to account for the case that the tablet of the index table has moved, right?","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/425333546/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"kmuthukk","id":13615376,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjE1Mzc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13615376?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk","html_url":"https://github.com/kmuthukk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmuthukk/gists{/g